WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:01.618
- I'm shook.

00:00:01.618 --> 00:00:04.785
(upbeat guitar music)

00:00:06.453 --> 00:00:08.377
- We're here to tell my daughter

00:00:08.377 --> 00:00:12.942
a secret that is probably
at this point 30 years old.

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:15.039
It's something that I think she'll find

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:16.608
surprising and out of character.

00:00:16.608 --> 00:00:18.240
- I feel like my kids always pretty much

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.308
know everything anyways,

00:00:19.308 --> 00:00:23.005
but this one secret has been
going on for quite a while.

00:00:23.005 --> 00:00:25.328
- He does some strange
stuff, it can be anything.

00:00:25.328 --> 00:00:26.684
- I mean, they know that I'm gay,

00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:29.783
but they don't know what that
means in my life, really.

00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.742
I've kind of kept them
sheltered from that.

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:33.454
- I don't know if that's true, but okay.

00:00:33.454 --> 00:00:37.167
He has a video on YouTube
called I'm Gay Gay.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.276
- I'm an open book with her.

00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:40.087
- I still feel like there's
a lot that I haven't

00:00:40.087 --> 00:00:42.219
heard about my dad, I'm gonna be honest.

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:43.177
- I don't know, I don't know.

00:00:43.177 --> 00:00:46.927
- I really feel like
there's some wild stuff.

00:00:49.442 --> 00:00:50.926
- No, I just need to tell him.

00:00:50.926 --> 00:00:55.394
You know that I've been
going to karaoke, right?

00:00:55.394 --> 00:00:56.853
- [Noah] You kinda stopped,
but I know that you--

00:00:56.853 --> 00:00:57.686
- I did stop.

00:00:57.686 --> 00:00:58.902
But like every Monday
I was going to karaoke.

00:00:58.902 --> 00:00:59.958
- [Noah] Yeah.

00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:02.312
- I'm a drag performer.

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:05.159
I have like a total drag persona.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:07.368
I know you know that I'm gay and that

00:01:07.368 --> 00:01:09.393
I dress up every once in a while.

00:01:09.393 --> 00:01:11.663
- And what's the name?

00:01:11.663 --> 00:01:12.700
- Herlinda.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.857
- Herlinda?

00:01:13.857 --> 00:01:15.114
- (laughter) Herlinda.

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:16.047
- I'm ready.
- You ready?

00:01:16.047 --> 00:01:17.213
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:01:17.213 --> 00:01:18.395
Being a doctor--
- Right.

00:01:18.395 --> 00:01:20.113
- You know that I told you
I always wanted to do it

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.687
from the time I was a little kid.

00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:22.520
- Yeah.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.353
- As long as I could possibly remember.

00:01:23.353 --> 00:01:24.186
- Yeah.

00:01:24.186 --> 00:01:25.019
- After the end of my second year,

00:01:25.019 --> 00:01:27.751
I had been named chief
resident for the third year.

00:01:27.751 --> 00:01:29.169
- Yeah!

00:01:29.169 --> 00:01:32.002
- And I quit the program entirely.

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:35.024
- What?

00:01:35.024 --> 00:01:35.857
- I quit.

00:01:36.745 --> 00:01:38.062
I resigned.

00:01:38.062 --> 00:01:40.008
I not only resigned from
being chief resident,

00:01:40.008 --> 00:01:42.758
I resigned from medicine, I quit.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.121
- Wait, are you kidding me?

00:01:45.121 --> 00:01:46.325
- [Steven] I'm not kidding you.

00:01:46.325 --> 00:01:47.158
- Woah!

00:01:48.426 --> 00:01:49.756
This is mind blowing!

00:01:49.756 --> 00:01:50.920
- And I had no idea what I was gonna do,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.446
I literally just couldn't take it anymore.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.865
- So then, so you quit, which is a word

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:58.016
that doesn't apply to him ever.

00:01:58.016 --> 00:01:59.182
- Do you wanna see her?

00:01:59.182 --> 00:02:00.015
- Sure.

00:02:00.903 --> 00:02:02.326
Oh man.

00:02:02.326 --> 00:02:04.122
You know, it's just not that surprising,

00:02:04.122 --> 00:02:06.676
because he used to do
drag every Halloween.

00:02:06.676 --> 00:02:09.076
- I just sat down and I
talked to mom about it,

00:02:09.076 --> 00:02:11.379
and I said, "You know, this
just doesn't feel right.

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:13.631
"But even though I'm miserable
and this is horrible,

00:02:13.631 --> 00:02:15.750
"it's just two more
years, I'm halfway done."

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.062
So when I came to them and said,

00:02:17.062 --> 00:02:20.145
"Look, I've reconsidered
and I'm gonna come back,"

00:02:20.145 --> 00:02:21.543
they were happy to have me back.

00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:23.878
- This is like a huge
chunk of family story

00:02:23.878 --> 00:02:25.304
that I've been missing.

00:02:25.304 --> 00:02:26.651
He just does a lot of things right,

00:02:26.651 --> 00:02:28.985
and I think my dad's
like the smartest person

00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:30.809
and the most dedicated person,

00:02:30.809 --> 00:02:33.430
so it's nice to know that
when he was around my age,

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:37.742
he did a really terrible,
made a really bad move.

00:02:37.742 --> 00:02:39.481
And you know what the biggest life lesson

00:02:39.481 --> 00:02:42.137
that my dad tells my
sister and I, don't quit.

00:02:42.137 --> 00:02:43.466
- Are you good?

00:02:43.466 --> 00:02:45.032
- I think I'm pretty good,

00:02:45.032 --> 00:02:46.674
I've got a little bit of a following.

00:02:46.674 --> 00:02:47.722
- Do I get to come now?

00:02:47.722 --> 00:02:48.864
- Yeah, you need to come.

00:02:48.864 --> 00:02:50.147
- I'll have to come see you do drag.

00:02:50.147 --> 00:02:52.683
- I feel like this is
my second coming out.

00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:54.941
But I appreciate that
you're not being judgmental.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.492
- Well, you aren't the
prettiest girl I'd ever seen,

00:02:57.492 --> 00:03:00.035
but you looked alright.
- It's gotten a lot better.

00:03:00.035 --> 00:03:01.087
- Better than that?

00:03:01.087 --> 00:03:03.270
- Rising from the dead,
as Taylor Swift says.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.163
- [Steven] Is that what she says?

00:03:04.163 --> 00:03:04.996
- Oh yes.

00:03:06.089 --> 00:03:07.289
- Yes.

00:03:07.289 --> 00:03:08.206
- Thoughts?

00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:11.596
- Oh, there was another secret?

00:03:11.596 --> 00:03:13.014
- Oh no, he likes Taylor Swift?

00:03:13.014 --> 00:03:14.405
(laughter)

00:03:14.405 --> 00:03:16.067
- No!

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.881
- I hate to tell you, but I'm a closet ...

00:03:18.881 --> 00:03:20.073
I have a playlist.

00:03:20.073 --> 00:03:21.779
I was gonna take mom to the show, yeah,

00:03:21.779 --> 00:03:24.341
when she tours for this album.

00:03:24.341 --> 00:03:25.581
- That's not a real thing.

00:03:25.581 --> 00:03:26.414
- Yes!

00:03:26.414 --> 00:03:27.247
- No!

00:03:27.247 --> 00:03:28.433
- I just hope he's good at it,

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:30.620
'cause it's a little bit more
embarrassing if he's bad.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.968
I need a good drag queen
dad, not a bad one.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.555
- Does this make you look at me different?

00:03:34.555 --> 00:03:35.388
- Yes.

00:03:35.388 --> 00:03:36.751
Just like, out of the
two people sitting here,

00:03:36.751 --> 00:03:39.122
who would you guess is the fan?

00:03:39.122 --> 00:03:41.219
- Bigger Taylor Swift fan?

00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:42.329
- It's good that it's out there,

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:44.617
but it feels a little strange.

00:03:44.617 --> 00:03:46.667
It was nice having my own little life.

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:47.701
- Basically what he just said is

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.152
the reason he didn't tell me

00:03:49.152 --> 00:03:51.769
is because he didn't want
me cramping his style.

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:52.933
- This was a good experience.

00:03:52.933 --> 00:03:53.766
- Oh yeah?

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.921
- I have plenty to use against you now.

00:03:54.921 --> 00:03:55.754
- Oh, okay.

00:03:55.754 --> 00:03:56.587
- A lot of ammo.

00:03:56.587 --> 00:03:57.420
- I am not embarrassed.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.330
- Oh, I think there will
probably still be more secrets.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.161
I think we can have our own lives.

00:04:01.161 --> 00:04:03.043
- You gotta keep secrets sometimes.

00:04:03.043 --> 00:04:05.626
(upbeat music)

